  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py` and a new test file, `tests/test_money.py`. The full suite passes: 11 tests, including the 5 new ones.\n\n`split` divides the amount evenly. Any leftover cents are added one each to the first elements, so `split(1000, 3)` gives `[334, 333, 333]`. If `parts` is below 1 it raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe new tests cover an even split, splits with a remainder, more parts than cents (`split(2, 4)` gives `[1, 1, 0, 0]`), a single part, and `parts` of 0 and -1.\n\nNegative amounts aren't tested. They still sum correctly, but the parts get rounded down, so `split(-5, 2)` returns `[-2, -3]`. The first element is the smaller one in size, the opposite of the positive case. If refunds should split as `[-3, -2]` instead, that's a small change.",
